# Engineering Standards

- Read the existing project shape before adding tools, frameworks, or conventions.
- Prefer TypeScript for application code unless the user chooses a different stack.
- Keep implementation choices boring and maintainable: small components, clear data models, and minimal dependencies.
- Do not put secrets, API keys, payment credentials, or production tokens in source files.
- Model money carefully: store prices in integer minor units where possible and display formatted currency at the edge.
- Validate transactional inputs on the server side when a backend exists.
- Add focused tests for cart math, promotions, checkout state, and any shared business logic.
- Preserve accessibility: semantic HTML, keyboard navigation, visible focus, labels, contrast, and useful alt text.
- Run the smallest meaningful verification after substantive changes and report anything not run.
